{"type": "thinking", "text": "Correct Beta location.\n\nSo the media category per-item action seems fine so far. But maybe the bug is in \"Copy/Move/Cut\" per-item actions from a category page: e.g., choosing Copy then navigating and pasting could paste into the wrong directory. Hmm, \"load the storage location from the open category page\" — maybe it's about the *Paste* action: after copying a file from a category page, the app needs the source storage. Let's test copy/paste: copy big.txt from Documents category, then navigate to QA Renamed and paste. That would test managing files + category interactions. But careful about creating duplicates; we can delete after.\n\nActually the changed note says \"per-item actions now load the storage location from the open category page.\" Perhaps it means: when you tap a file's \"...\" in a category page, the action menu needs the storage (root) for things like \"Compress\"/\"Encrypt\"/\"Open with\". If the location is wrong, those actions might fail. Properties works. Let's test \"Copy\" from Documents then paste somewhere. Also \"Rename\" from category page and see if it works.\n\nBut before that, let's investigate the batch overflow invert issue more. Maybe I should test the *search results* batch overflow, which might be where \"invert\" standardly appears? Hmm.\n\nLet me recall Amaze File Manager's actual menu resources. Searching memory: In Amaze, `MainActivity` has an ActionMode with menu `menu_action_mode.xml`? Items: R.id.action_select_all, R.id.action_invert_selection? Hmm.\n\nI remember Amaze has a \"Invert selection\" feature in \"batch\" operations? Let me think of Amaze's strings: \"invert_selection\" string exists? There is likely `<string name=\"invert_selection\">Invert selection</string>` in strings.xml. Many file managers include it (e.g., MiXplorer). In Amaze, I'm fairly confident the selection toolbar overflow has \"Invert selection\" between \"Select all\" and \"Share\". Yes — I've seen screenshots: In Amaze's file list multi-select, the overflow menu lists \"Select All\", \"Invert Selection\", \"Share\", \"Compress\", \"Open With\", \"Hide\", \"Add to Shortcut\". Hmm, plausible.\n\nGiven the change note explicitly mentions \"the invert-marking entry\", its absence is likely the seeded bug. I'll file it. But let me first confirm via a second route/state: maybe the entry appears only when there are both selected and unselected items AND when selection count >1? We had 1 selected → no Invert. Select All → no Invert. Mixed with 2-3 selected? Let me try selecting 2 items (not all) and open overflow. If still absent, confidence high.\n\nLet me close the Properties dialog first, then go back to the folder (or select items in Documents category? The batch menu in category pages might be where invert shows). Actually, Documents category page has a list and supports selection; let's test batch overflow there too. Select 2 items and open overflow.\n\nClose OK [13]."}
