{"type": "thinking", "text": "The copy from the Documents category worked: notes.txt pasted into QA Renamed (15 B). So per-item copy works correctly and the source storage path was correct. The navigation drawer media category per-item action is fine in this respect.\n\nNow clean up: delete the pasted notes.txt from QA Renamed (it's a duplicate; original remains in Amaze). Actually, deleting it is a data change but reverts our test. We should delete the test folder QA Renamed entirely at the end (including big.txt and notes.txt copy).\n\nBefore cleanup, continue tests:\n\n1. Test text viewer with multi-line file / large? Our big.txt now 14.6KB, all ASCII single line. Let's test the tail with \"Find in page\" to be sure the tail loaded (we saw it). Maybe test the find function works.\n\n2. Test batch invert in this folder (QA Renamed, 2 files) — maybe with 2 files it's the same as before.\n\nLet me now step back and plan remaining tests and bug reports.\n\nRemaining areas to exercise:\n- Navigation drawer: quick access pencil icons editing (this might be \"per-item actions\" too!). Let's test the pencil action: it opens a dialog to edit quick access item (name/location). The change note says \"per-item actions now load the storage location from the open category page.\" Hmm, the pencil icon is a per-item action in the drawer. It loads the storage location... Wait! Maybe \"Navigation drawer media categories: per-item actions\" means for each drawer item (DCIM, Download, ...), the pencil action loads the *quick access entry's stored location* (the path) — and now it loads \"the storage location from the open category page\"? That doesn't parse.\n\nHmm, consider: The drawer list includes the storage volume(s). Per-item actions on the *media categories*... Actually, maybe the change is: the media category items (Images, Videos, Audio, Documents, APKs) now can have per-item actions (like \"Set as home\"?). No.\n\nMaybe the intended test is simply: open drawer → Images → open a file's actions → Properties → location correct. We did that. Good.\n\n- Text viewer: open/preview text files. We tested notes, report+final, readme (Alpha, Beta), big.txt 14.6KB. Need to check editing/save/persistence (we did; file persisted after re-entry). Also test \"Find in page\" (search) maybe. And test file content with multi-line/Unicode.\n\n- Managing files in a folder: create folder (validated), rename folder, delete, copy/paste (done), move/cut (not tested), batch selection actions (copy/delete/cut), show hidden, sort maybe. We should test delete (on our test data), cut/move, and maybe batch delete. Also test rename of a file, select-all, etc.\n\nLet's do a few of these systematically to satisfy the sweep, focusing on finding real bugs.\n\nFirst, the missing \"Invert selection\" — I want to be more certain. Let me check the Amaze app's normal (non-selection) overflow in a folder that has items: it showed Sort, History, Grid View, Hidden Files, Set As Home, Open in Terminal, Exit. No Select All. In selection mode overflow: Select All / Share / Compress / Open with / Hide / Add Shortcut (real folder), or Select All/Hide (category). Hmm, where would Invert be? If the app has an \"Invert selection\" string, it should be in the selection overflow. Its absence in both menus is suspicious. But maybe the version 3.11.3 doesn't have invert at all, and the change note is a red herring? The change note says \"the invert-marking entry is now handled entirely inside the list adapter.\" That means before, it was handled by the activity and now by the adapter. The entry should exist.\n\nHmm, wait: maybe \"invert-marking\" refers to marking files (selection) via *long press* and the \"invert marking\" is done by tapping an item's checkbox? In Amaze's list, selected items show a checkmark. \"Invert marking\" might be the action that inverts selection; the menu entry name could be \"Invert selection\". I'm fairly confident.\n\nLet me search the web from memory: Amaze File Manager FAQ: \"How do I select multiple files? Long press... tap the overflow menu to select all or invert selection.\" I think yes, Amaze's multi-select overflow does include \"Invert selection\". I'll report it.\n\nActually, let me test the search-results batch menu too, since Amaze's search results may show an \"Invert selection\" entry (the adapter for search results). The change says \"handled entirely inside the list adapter\" — the list adapter is the same for the main list. Hmm, but maybe the \"batch overflow menu\" is in the search results screen. The \"search results\" screen in Amaze has selection mode with its own overflow? Let's check: search for \"readme\" from the Amaze folder and see the results list, long-press to select, and check the overflow menu. This is worth testing because the missing entry might appear there (if the adapter adds it). Also tests navigation/search (not in scope, but related).\n\nLet me first clean up our test copy (notes.txt in QA Renamed) and maybe keep big.txt for later text tests. Actually we'll keep QA Renamed for now (delete at end).\n\nLet me test the batch overflow in this folder with 2 items (big.txt, notes.txt): long-press big.txt, tap notes.txt, open overflow. We know the real-folder menu shows Select All, Share, Compress, Open with, Hide, Add Shortcut. Hmm, no Invert. We already tested in Amaze folder. No need to repeat.\n\nMaybe the missing entry is actually \"Add to Bookmarks\"? No.\n\nOK let me file the invert report now (using the Amaze folder state I observed). I need to cite the exact screen: \"selection mode overflow menu in /storage/emulated/0/AndroidQA/Amaze shows Select All, Share, Compress, Open with, Hide, Add Shortcut but no Invert selection.\" For the element_ref, I need a current observation. Right now the screen is the QA Renamed folder with 2 files, no menu open. Let me open selection mode and the overflow again to have a fresh element ref for the menu. Then file the report.\n\nActually, the file_report takes element_ref from latest observe. The \"missing\" element doesn't exist; the closest is the overflow menu itself. I can point at the overflow menu item \"Select All\" or the \"More options\" button. For a missing entry, the closest element might be the overflow menu. I'll use the \"More options\" element in selection mode.\n\nLet me reproduce in QA Renamed: long-press big.txt, tap notes, overflow."}
