re sense: \"invert-marking\" might mean the marking toggle (invert = toggle the marked state). The \"entry\" though...\n\nLet me reconsider the sentence: \"Batch overflow menu: the invert-marking entry is now handled entirely inside the list adapter.\" Maybe originally the overflow menu had an \"Invert selection\" entry handled by activity->adapter; now the adapter handles it. If the dev says \"could not reproduce\", either the bug report is invalid (no invert entry in this build at all) or the reproduction conditions are different (e.g., the entry only appears in a batch menu somewhere else).\n\nMaybe the \"batch overflow menu\" is the menu accessible via the *checkbox* long-press? Hmm.\n\nLet me investigate the app UI more: Is there a \"batch\" feature? In Amaze, there's \"Batch rename\" maybe in selection overflow (\"Rename\" for multiple files). Our batch overflow with 2 files didn't show Rename. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the batch overflow menu is in the **search results** screen where a different overflow appears. Let me check the search results selection overflow. Also, the \"Recent files\" page might have a different batch menu.\n\nLet me search: use the search icon, query \"readme\", then long-press a result and open overflow.\n\nActually — hold on. Maybe the \"invert-marking entry\" appears in the **overflow menu of the FAB**? No.\n\nLet me look at the app's implemented menu items in various selection contexts. The main list selection overflow shows those 6. The category page showed 2. Search results might show more/different.\n\nLet me test search results selection overflow.\n\nFirst exit selection (Done), then tap search [1], type \"readme\"."}
