on mode**. Tap [10] (row's properties button) while selected could open a batch menu with \"Invert selection\"? Let me test: enter selection mode and tap the row's \"...\" button (not long-press). It might show per-item actions (Open with, Cut, Copy, ...). Hmm, that's per-item, not batch.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the \"batch overflow\" is in the **\"Recent files\" page** or **\"Images\" category**, which uses a different adapter (the \"list adapter\" might be `ExplorerAdapter` vs `TabFragment`). Hmm.\n\nHold on — maybe \"invert-marking entry\" refers to the **\"Invert selection\" in the long-press context menu of the *home screen card*?** No.\n\nLet me look at Amaze's actual UI docs. Amaze file manager multi-select: \"Long press on a file/folder to select. Tap other items to add. In the action bar, you can copy, cut, delete. The overflow menu has Select all / Deselect all, Share, Compress, Open with, Hide, Add shortcut.\" Hmm, maybe \"Invert selection\" exists only in the \"batch rename\" dialog? Hmm.\n\nActually, I now recall in Amaze (3.x), there is indeed an \"Invert selection\" item in the overflow menu when searching? No...\n\nLet me consider that the developer's \"could not reproduce\" may mean my report was inaccurate in the *expected* behavior: perhaps the invert entry is not expected in this menu at all. The instruction says a developer will reply; \"could not reproduce\" is a rejection. I should not re-report without evidence. Maybe the seeded bug is elsewhere in that area: e.g., an existing entry like \"Select All\" works incorrectly when marks exist (invert semantics?). Let's test the batch operations themselves for bugs:\n- \"Select All\" then \"Deselect All\": does the count/marks update correctly?\n- \"Select All\" while some selected.\n- Copy/Cut with multiple selection: do all files copy/move?\n- Delete with multiple selection (with confirmation).\n- Share/Compress with multiple.\n\n\"the invert-marking entry is now handled entirely inside the list adapter\" — maybe the bug is in the \"Select All\"/\"Deselect All\" behavior? Hmm no.\n\nWait wait. Maybe \"invert-marking\" is not \"Invert selection\" but refers to the **\"mark as\"** action? In Amaze, there might be an overflow entry \"Mark as\" (mark all, invert marks) in the **\"Cloud Connection\"**? Hmm.\n\nLet me search the app's UI text through the accessibility tree for \"Invert\". We could use the app's search? No, that searches files.\n\nWhat about the FAB \"more\" menu? It has New Folder, New File, Cloud Connection. The Cloud Connection (SMB/FTP) setup may have \"invert\"? no.\n\nAlternative: Use the overflow menu in a folder list when *no* items are selected? It showed Sort/History/Grid/Hidden/Set As Home/Open in Terminal/Exit — no invert.\n\nHmm, could \"batch overflow menu\" be the overflow **inside the batch rename dialog**? There's no such dialog in our menu.\n\nMaybe the menu in the selection mode is scrollable and there are more items below \"Add Shortcut\"? In screenshots, the popup had exactly 6 items ending at Add Shortcut; the popup height was around y=800 with the items fitting. No scroll indicator. So no.\n\nOK, let me set this aside and continue with other tests. Maybe I mis-assumed; perhaps the seeded bug for the batch menu is that **\"Select All\"/\"Deselect All\" doesn't persist after rotating** or that the marks aren't cleared when leaving selection mode (state bug). Let me test state/reversal on selection:\n1. Select all, rotate device, see if selection preserved and menu still works.\n2. Enter selection, mark 1, press back/done, re-enter selection: marks cleared? (Should be cleared.)\n3. Tap \"Deselect All\" then check count 0 and toolbar exits? \n\nLet me test these quickly. First rotate while in selection mode with 2 marked. This tests device rotation.\n\nLet me enter selection, mark both, rotate landscape, observe."}
