ect all again → Copy (clipboard = new whole content, ~29KB)\n- Tap near start → long-press → Paste → doubles to 58KB\n- Select all → Copy → tap → paste → 116KB\n- Save\nThen close and reopen; check tail marker appears (search? we can look at observed end) and file size via properties.\n\nEach select-all/copy/paste sequence is ~5 calls. 3 rounds ~15 calls + save + reopen + check ~20. Let's do it.\n\nBut note: pasting near start inserts at a word-selected location, potentially replacing a word. That's fine. And \"Select all\" selects the whole content; \"Copy\" copies it; tapping near start deselects/moves cursor; long-press selects a word and shows toolbar with Paste; tapping Paste replaces that word with the clipboard content (adding full content minus word). Growth is essentially doubling.\n\nWait, in the previous paste, the observed content: the pasted clipboard was inserted at the tap position (not replacing? it looked like insertion). Actually the text showed \"...0123456789|CURSOR-TEST||BLOCK2...\" — the content after tap position was replaced? Let me analyze: Before paste, text = \"[prefix ~858 chars]START|...|VERY-END-MARK|\" where prefix started with \"|CURSOR-TEST||BLOCK2-START|...\". Hmm, the tap at (60,300) placed cursor at position 0? Then paste inserted at 0. But the observed after paste starts with \"|CURSOR-TEST||BLOCK2-START|0123...\" — same as before (no duplicate at start). Then later I see the duplicate in the middle: after \"...|CHUNK1|...|VERY-END-MARK|\" there's \"0123...|THE-END-OF-FILE|...|VERY-END-MARK|\". Hmm, that suggests the paste was inserted at the *middle*, not start. The displayed text is confusing due to possible middle truncation by the observe.\n\nRegardless, the file size went from 7301+858=8159? Wait, before paste: after typing BLOCK2, size was 7301. Hmm, 7301 included BLOCK2 (~858) — so before BLOCK2 the file was 6443; after CURSOR-TEST (13) = 6456; after BLOCK2 (if ~845 chars) = 7301. Then paste of the 7301-char clipboard should give ~14602 — matching the 14.60 kB listing. Good. So paste added exactly the clipboard.\n\nSo doubling works.\n\nLet's navigate to QA Renamed and open big.txt. Current screen: \"No Terminal Apps installed\" dialog. Close OK [2], then tap QA Renamed, big.txt."}
