** category for keep.jpg → \"keep2.jpg\" and check the real Amaze folder. If the rename fails there too, it's a reproducible bug (\"per-item Rename from category pages does nothing\"). Then we can report with strong evidence. But changing keep.jpg name then back is risky; if rename fails, nothing changes (good). If it succeeds, rename back. Let's instead use our own big.txt (test data) as we did. The rename failed; to reproduce, rename from category again and check once more; maybe the first failure was a fluke (e.g., stale list after all, but the folder listing said big.txt...). \n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider: could the rename have happened but then the listing showed the old name because of caching, and then our navigation to QA Renamed also showed a cached listing? The fullpath header said QA Renamed, and the folder listing showed big.txt. The app's listing comes from a filesystem scan; caching could persist within a fragment instance but we created a new fragment by navigating. So it should be fresh. Unless the fragment instance was restored from a saved state (same tab) and didn't rescan. Hmm, navigating from root to QA Renamed creates a new MainFragment, scans the directory. It showed big.txt — so the file is still named big.txt.\n\nTo be extra sure, let's check the file's Properties from the real folder: if it's big.txt with 14.60 kB, then rename definitely failed. We already saw the row \"big.txt | 14.60 kB\". Good.\n\nSo there's a bug: Rename from the Documents category page appeared to succeed (dialog closed) but the file name did not change. Let me reproduce once more with big.txt (now in QA Renamed) from the Documents category. This is a good candidate for area #3.\n\nActually hold on — maybe the rename failed because the target \"big2.txt\" already existed in the same directory... it doesn't. Or because the source file was in a folder with spaces (\"QA Renamed\") and the path handling broke? The Properties showed the correct path, though. Hmm, maybe the rename dialog for a category file sets the parent using the *category* path (e.g., \"Documents/big.txt\") instead of the real path. Then rename would try to rename a non-existent file and fail.\n\nLet me reproduce with another file from the same folder, notes.txt (copy in QA Renamed) — ambiguous. Better big.txt again: rename to \"big9.txt\" from Documents category, then check the real folder. If it fails again, report.\n\nLet's navigate back to Documents (drawer), then per-item Rename big.txt → big9.txt. Actually, we're in QA Renamed now. Open drawer → Documents."}
