more thing: press the row in the category page \"renametest.txt\" — if it opens, its path is real. Then rename from the *real folder* (works). Fine.\n\nI'm fairly convinced this is a real bug. But the developer rejected it. Maybe I should report it with more precise steps and point at the category page list (which still shows renametest.txt after SAVE) rather than the real folder. The report tool says a report about missing thing may omit quote; for no_effect, quote should show the defect. The category list showing \"renametest.txt\" after the rename is the evidence. Let me re-file with the category page as the screen and element \"renametest.txt row in Documents category\", observed_quote \"renametest.txt\", expected the row to show renamedok.txt. Also mention the dialog close + file unchanged. But filing the same bug twice might be annoying; however, the first report may have been rejected due to ambiguity (I referenced big.txt and the real folder). Let me try once more with the simpler reproduction.\n\nActually, before that, let me test whether the rename from the *real folder* works on renametest.txt (to confirm the app's rename works at all, isolating the category page). Rename renametest.txt → renamedok.txt in QA Renamed; verify it changes. Then rename back or delete. This will strengthen the comparison: same file, same app, rename works in the real folder but not in the category page.\n\nLet's do: in QA Renamed, per-item overflow of renametest.txt [16] → Rename → renamedok.txt → SAVE → observe the list."}
